(Bug #95. A name declared without a type noun is a statically-typed name
 like any other, so `NAME's type` names that type and says `(static)` -
 LANGUAGE.md: a variable reports `(static)` "because the compiler knows the
 type from the declaration", and only a `value` reports `(dynamic)`. These
 answered off a runtime tag byte nothing but a `value` ever writes, so a
 text called itself a Number and every one of them said `(dynamic)`.)

a text called declared is "hello".
Print declared's type.

Set label to "hello".
Print label's type.

